[
    {
        "content": "<p>This just confused me (and thanks to Claude for solving):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/--</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">error: failed to synthesize</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">  Foo Unit</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">Hint: Additional diagnostic information may be available using the `set_option diagnostics true` command.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I had imagined that <code>scoped</code> here would scope the instance to the <code>Foo</code> namespace, but in fact it scopes it to <code>Foo.Bar</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- now works</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This tripped me up with <code>Foo := DirectSum</code>, <code>Bar := GradeZero</code>, and the instance (from mathlib) being </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">priority</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">900</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GradeZero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which when I <code>scoped</code> it in the <code>DirectSum</code> namespace, suddenly made semirings fail to synthesize in the file, because I had not written <code>open scoped GradeZero</code>. My instinct is that I would like the instance to be called <code>DirectSum.GradeZero.semiring</code> but I would like it scoped to the <code>DirectSum</code> namespace, so I am going for</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">priority</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">900</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GradeZero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Semiring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">blah</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">900</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">GradeZero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">semiring</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which does what I want, and looks confusing (\"why scope twice?\") but I've added a comment. The first scoping scoped it to <code>DirectSum.GradeZero</code>, the second to <code>DirectSum</code>. Just flagging in case this was unindented at core's end.</p>",
        "id": 598709628,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1780139682
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Why not get rid of the instance name and use the auto-generated name?</p>",
        "id": 598713364,
        "sender_full_name": "Jovan Gerbscheid",
        "timestamp": 1780142747
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't name them, I was just scoping them. Sounds like a good idea to me.</p>",
        "id": 598731917,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1780158425
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Instead of scoping the first time, why not just make it a <code>def</code>? I assume you don't really want an instance in <code>DirectSum.GradeZero</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">attribute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: Bar.inst -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 598741072,
        "sender_full_name": "Arend Mellendijk",
        "timestamp": 1780165306
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah I know there's plenty of ways to work around this behaviour, the question is simply whether this is expected behaviour which is why I'm asking it in <a class=\"stream\" data-stream-id=\"270676\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4\">#lean4</a> .</p>",
        "id": 598799254,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1780170254
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, this is a footgun! Remember that</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">attributes</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">modifiers</span><span class=\"bp\">/&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">baz</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is a macro that expands to</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">attributes</span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"n\">modifiers</span><span class=\"bp\">/&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">command</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baz</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><del>This also means that if you made it a <code>local instance</code>, it would only be an instance until the end of the namespace <code>Bar</code>, not the rest of your file.</del> (EDIT: see below)</p>",
        "id": 599851659,
        "sender_full_name": "Floris van Doorn",
        "timestamp": 1780504123
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That last part isn't true. There's internal <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/fd009949156901e6cf15b6d9bf1122294b8e697a/src/Lean/Parser/Command.lean#L340-L350\"><code>end_local_scope</code></a> syntax which is supposed to mitigate exactly this by preventing local attributes from going out of scope in scopes introduced by macros (like <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/fd009949156901e6cf15b6d9bf1122294b8e697a/src/Lean/Elab/Declaration.lean#L145-L158\">this</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/fd009949156901e6cf15b6d9bf1122294b8e697a/src/Lean/Elab/BuiltinCommand.lean#L532-L536\"><code>in</code></a>). And indeed this works for <code>local</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inst</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: Bar.inst -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">synth</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599966761,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1780537176
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It does feel pretty weird that it doesn't change the scope <code>scoped</code> attributes are attached to though</p>",
        "id": 599967391,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1780537562
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the correction!</p>",
